diff --git a/docs/user/advanced.rst b/docs/user/advanced.rst
index f5209a5..38bcdea 100644
--- a/docs/user/advanced.rst
+++ b/docs/user/advanced.rst
@@ -1120,6 +1120,22 @@ coffee.
 
     r = requests.get('https://github.com', timeout=None)
 
+If you make many requests through one :class:`Session <requests.Session>`, set
+a default timeout on it once instead of repeating ``timeout=`` on every call.
+Every request sent through the session, including requests made while following
+redirects, uses it unless the call passes its own ``timeout``::
+
+    s = requests.Session()
+    s.timeout = (3.05, 27)
+
+    s.get('https://github.com')              # uses (3.05, 27)
+    s.get('https://github.com', timeout=60)  # this call waits up to 60 seconds
+
+Session defaults follow the same rule as the other session settings: passing
+``timeout=None`` to a call means "not set here", so the session's default still
+applies. To make a single call wait forever despite a session default, pass
+``timeout=(None, None)``.
+
 .. note:: The connect timeout applies to each connection attempt to an IP address.
           If multiple addresses exist for a domain name, the underlying ``urllib3`` will
           try each address sequentially until one successfully connects.
